      "math_academy_id": "e-16429",
      "problem": "The table below gives the values of $x$ that satisfy $P(X\\geq x) = p,$ where $X\\sim \\chi^2(k).$ Given that the random variable $X \\sim \\chi^2(7),$ find the value of $x$ such that $P(X \\geq x) = 0.99.$\n\n| $k \\setminus p$ | $0.995$ | $0.990$ | $0.975$ | $0.950$ | $0.900$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $5$ | $\\,0.412\\,$ | $\\,0.554\\,$ | $\\,0.831\\,$ | $\\,1.145\\,$ | $\\,1.610\\,$ |\n| $6$ | $\\,0.676\\,$ | $\\,0.872\\,$ | $\\,1.237\\,$ | $\\,1.635\\,$ | $\\,2.204\\,$ |\n| $7$ | $\\,0.989\\,$ | $\\,1.239\\,$ | $\\,1.690\\,$ | $\\,2.167\\,$ | $\\,2.833\\,$ |",
      "worked_solution": "Since $X \\sim \\chi^2(7),$ we focus on the row of the table that corresponds to $k=7.$\n\n| $k \\setminus p$ | $0.995$ | $0.990$ | $0.975$ | $0.950$ | $0.900$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $7$ | $\\,0.989\\,$ | $\\,1.239\\,$ | $\\,1.690\\,$ | $\\,2.167\\,$ | $\\,2.833\\,$ |\n\nFrom this row, we see that\n\n$$\nP(X \\geq 1.239) = 0.990.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our answer is $x=1.239.$",
